WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
An AI model decoded chest x-rays from 3.67 million people and predicted multiple cancers, at least one year before diagnosis. This is Planetterrian Daily, episode 190. A new paper in Nature argues that artificial intelligence now operates as a determinant of health. The author's frame AI systems as active influences on health outcomes through data interpretation and decision support. The argument rests on how AI models

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.120
process clinical information at scale across large populations.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:39.840
The paper calls for treating AI as a distinct factor alongside traditional determinants,

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.620
such as genetics and environment.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:48.580
It positions AI alongside established categories like socio-economic status and lifestyle behaviors

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:49.560
in health models.

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:56.960
Next up, a multimodal AI model named Ankoformer examined electronic health records and chest

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:03.440
X-rays from 3.67 million individuals. The model predicted cancer at least one year before

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:09.620
clinical diagnosis across multiple cancer types. Area under the receiver operating characteristic

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:18.140
curve reached 0.869 for all cancers combined. Performance reached 0.905 for cervical cancer

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:25.840
and 0.896 for colon cancers specifically. The study appears in an open access cell press journal

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.300
and includes detailed validation metrics.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:31.280
On a different note, a leading publisher states

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.340
that open scientific collaboration remains essential

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:35.520
for continued progress.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.240
The statement emphasizes shared data

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:41.400
and joint projects across borders as core requirements.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.320
The publisher notes that closed system slow discovery rates

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:47.300
and limit verification opportunities.

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:49.440
The comments appear in coverage

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.100
of current publishing practices

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.800
and international data sharing.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:59.820
Shifting focus. A new Australian Institute will convert research breakthroughs into treatments for brain disorders.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:06.680
The facility focuses on translating laboratory findings into clinical applications for neurological conditions.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:13.220
Organizers aim to accelerate development of therapies through structured partnerships with existing research centers.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:18.920
The announcement highlights dedicated infrastructure for moving discoveries from bench to bedside.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:24.680
Wells, MesserSmith, MD, has assumed leadership of the CU and Shoots Cancer Center.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:30.060
MesserSmith stated that the center's impact will be broad and transformative across

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:31.220
research and care.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:36.960
The appointment emphasizes expanded research programs alongside enhanced patient care

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:37.440
initiatives.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:43.440
The center plans new initiatives focused on cancer prevention strategies and novel treatment

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:44.120
protocols.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:50.320
Theoretical physicist Quarenten Laudicina studied how materials form glass during controlled

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:51.360
cooling processes.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:56.660
The work reveals self-limiting particle clusters that form during the transition to the

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:57.520
glassy state.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:02.960
These clusters explain why certain liquids resist crystallization even at low temperatures.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:08.740
The findings connect everyday observations of glass behavior to underlying molecular physics

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:09.380
mechanisms.

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:16.200
The Sun follows an 11-year cycle of active and quiet phases driven by magnetic field dynamics.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:22.180
Quiet periods feature reduced magnetic turbulence and fewer sunspots visible on the surface.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:28.620
Accurate prediction of cycle intensity affects satellite operations and power grid stability worldwide.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:35.220
Observations since the 1800s have documented the repeating pattern with increasing precision over time.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:40.760
A pulmonologist warns that new wellness claims for nicotine lack supporting long-term

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:41.300
evidence.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:46.280
The column highlights established risks to lung health from increased exposure through

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.560
various delivery methods.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.960
The author notes that marketing often omits documented respiratory effects observed in

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:54.020
clinical populations.

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:59.340
Current claims focus on cognitive or mood benefits without controlled data spanning

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:00.260
multiple years.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:06.740
Fibrobiologics is developing fibroblast-based approaches to restore thymic function in aging

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:12.960
individuals. The thymus typically converts to fat by age 60, reducing immune training capacity

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:19.220
over time. The company uses fibroblasts rather than stem cells to address age-related decline in

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:25.640
organ structure. The strategy aims to improve immune cell selection processes and reduce infection

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.360
susceptibility in older adults.

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:33.840
Aspen neuroscience is testing an autologous IPSC derived therapy in a clinical trial

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.040
for Parkinson's disease.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:41.380
Patient skin cells are reprogrammed to induced pleuropotin stem cells and then differentiated

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.320
into dopamine neuron precursors.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:49.800
The company has received fast track and RMAT designations from the FDA to expedite development.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:57.280
Genomic and transcriptomic assays verify cell identity and safety profiles before transplantation procedures.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:04.760
Union Minister Jitendra Singh stated that India is entering a new era of genomics and gene therapy applications.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:11.080
The remarks highlight growing national capacity in genetic medicine through expanded laboratory infrastructure.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:17.100
Government support includes dedicated research facilities and specialized training programs for researchers.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:17.280
measures.

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:22.760
The comments position India among countries actively scaling gene-based interventions for

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:23.560
clinically use.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:28.660
Eight common preservatives in processed foods associate with higher rates of high blood

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:30.820
pressure and cardiovascular disease.

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:36.880
The observational study examined dietary patterns alongside clinical outcome records in large

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:37.420
cohorts.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:42.740
Heavy consumption correlated with elevated cardiovascular risk markers across multiple

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:44.300
population subgroups.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:49.320
Researchers note that causation cannot be established from the current observational design

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:49.780
alone.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:57.000
Researchers propose that the Kumran sect used a 364-day calendar structured around 52 weeks.

00:05:57.640 --> 00:06:02.400
The system kept holidays on fixed weekdays, but drifted relative to solar seasons over

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:03.300
successive years.

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:08.640
The finding aligns with the sect's documented practices preserved in surviving manuscript

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:09.120
fragments.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:15.700
The calendar's structure explains inconsistencies noted in earlier historical and textual analyses.

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:22.320
Isotope ratios in Tyrannosaurus rex teeth indicate body temperatures comparable to those of elephants.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:28.600
The data suggests active internal temperature regulation rather than passive environmental matching.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:34.580
The measurements come from well-preserved dental enamel samples recovered from multiple fossil sites.

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:40.120
The results challenge earlier assumptions about dinosaur thermal regulation based on

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:41.480
modern reptile models.

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:47.040
Researchers identified the genetic source of a rare blood antigen through targeted genomic

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:47.580
analysis.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:53.500
The discovery establishes a previously unrecognized blood group system with distinct inheritance

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:53.980
patterns.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:07:00.060
The work relied on genomic sequencing of individuals carrying the antigen across multiple families.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:04.840
studies. The finding improves compatibility matching protocols for transfusion medicine

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:10.240
in clinical settings. Most people assume dinosaurs behave like modern reptiles and could

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.140
not maintain steady internal heat.

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:18.800
Fossil tooth enamel tells a different story. Isotope ratios in T-Rex teeth match temperatures

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:24.580
near those of living elephants, indicating active metabolic heat production. Right now,

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:29.580
every mammal listener maintains core temperature through mitochondrial activity in muscle and

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:35.120
organ tissue. The same chemical signatures that distinguish warm from cold metabolisms in

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:40.940
living species can be read in teeth that are millions of years old. One memorable detail is

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:46.740
that the measured temperatures sit within a few degrees of 37 degrees Celsius. Future isotope

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:51.600
work on additional dinosaur species will show whether this pattern was widespread or limited

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:56.940
to large predators. Before we go, keep an eye on further validation studies of the

00:07:56.940 --> 00:08:01.060
oncoformer model, as independent groups apply it to new populations.

